# Relay Stop Rule

Stop at **65–70% capacity**. PASS is success, not failure. Pleasure, not pressure.

A seat that stops cleanly at the right moment is more valuable than one that pushes to 100% and leaves the next seat in a mess.

---

## Stop triggers — exit when any one applies

- Next step requires verification you have not done (Beast health, HEAD state, PII model behaviour)
- You would have to guess repo structure or API shape
- One PR-sized slice is complete and fresh eyes add more value than continued momentum
- Attention is fuzzy on preconditions — you are making assumptions you cannot verify

---

## PASS protocol

At seat end, in order:

1. Update `05-pass.md` — set `done_this_seat`, `next_seat_should`, `blockers`
2. Fill Vellum `preform-seat-pass` — see `vellum-witness` rule
3. Write the baton (see below)

No session ends without all three.

---

## Baton

The baton is the handoff document for your next self (or the next seat).
Write it thinking about what you would want to read if you were starting cold.

Required content:
- What was done this seat (verified delta, not intentions)
- What is open (unfinished, parked, or blocked)
- What the next seat needs to know — repo state, gotchas, decisions made, context that is not in the code
- Any blockers with enough detail to unblock without re-investigation

Undone is a valid baton state. Write it up honestly. All outcomes — complete, partial, blocked — go to Linear and Vellum.
